MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977144-097-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977144-097', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Closing review: Priya back to full duty since March 18, no f/u needed. Board closed the case, nothing open. No activity in 60 days, closing diary. Treated at Empire Physical Medicine, released, no restr. If Priya calls with a flare up, reopen and send back to Dr Okafor. All bills paid, nothing pending. Final med report rec\'d, contusion resolved. Total paid on the file approx $4,500.\nDOI December 26, Priya tripped on something on the floor and went down at service site. First seen at Empire Physical Medicine on December 30, dx contusion of the neck and low back, lumbar xray no acute findings. On modified duty from December 29. Back to full duty from February 22. PT at Riverbend Physical Therapy started January 12, 12 of 12 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered January 26, result February 7: Mild disc bulge L4-5, no stenosis. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $1,415 paid to date. Contacts: Adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Paula Nakamura, ER supervisor Tasha Okafor, treating Dr Okafor, PT Victor Haddad at Riverbend Physical Therapy. Coverage: Wegmans Food Markets on the risk, Monroe county, service site.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 1136, n.word_count = 190;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977156-004-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977156-004', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'ran prior claims for Emma Rivera, none found. -Tina', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 51, n.word_count = 9;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977156-005-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977156-005', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'New assignment , DOI 12/21/2025 at operations facility. IW says she missed last few steps and fell at operations facility. sx: pain in the low back, worse by end of shift. treating at North Shore Occupational Health w/ DR Haddad. employer sent C-2F, rec\'d 12/25/2025. dx per first visit: strain. C-3 not yet rec\'d. will call IW and employer today. we have not rec\'d any wage info yet. employer says IW has worked there a while, no prior injuries per Tasha Kowalski. coverage confirmed, State Insurance Fund is on risk. we need job description and wage statement from employer. claim # 6977156, Queens county.\nDOI 12/21/2025, IW missed the last few steps and fell at operations facility. Off work from 12/22/25. Lena Alvarez is the worker\'s attorney', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 748, n.word_count = 127;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977156-006-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977156-006', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'per email, will f/u\nFrom: Tasha Kowalski <tasha@harborviewcommunityhealth.example>\nSent: Tue, Dec 23, 2025 17:22\nTo: Marcus Hill\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977156 - Rivera\n\nHi Marcus,\nWe can offer light duty starting 01/03/2026, 4 hrs/day.\nPlease confirm whether the clami has been accepted.\nPlease send us the restrictions in writing.\n\nRegards,\nTasha Kowalski', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 353, n.word_count = 52;
