MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977160-080-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977160-080', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'File review April 13. Chloe has a strain of the low back, hip and both knees from December 9, claim is scheduled for a hearing. Chloe is seeing Dr Haddad at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center and last reported pain at 0/10, no complaints. Restr are: Released to full duty, no restr. Chloe is working regular duty, no issues. No lost time and no wage payments due. Pending: Nothing. Plan: Continue to monitor, next review April 27.\nDOI December 9, Chloe was hit at an intersection driving the company vehicle at warehouse. First seen at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center on 12/12/25, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. On modified duty from December 10. Back to full duty from February 18.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 728, n.word_count = 130;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977160-081-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977160-081', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'April 16 reserves - Daniel\'s file: med reserve $6000. ok to keep the reserve as is. we should revisit after next medical', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 120, n.word_count = 22;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977160-082-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977160-082', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Subject: Status Report - Claim 6977160 - Chloe Nguyen\nHi Dev,\n\nPlease see the update below on Chloe Nguyen\'s claim (City Operations Department, DOI 12-9-2025, warehouse). I have kept the history short, call me if you want more.\n\nCLAIM HISTORY\nDOI December 9, Chloe Nguyen was hit at an intersection driving the company vehicle at warehouse. First seen at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center on December 12, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. On modified duty from December 10. Back to full duty from 02/18/2026. MRI ordered January 7, result January 18: mild disc bulge L4-5, no stenosis. IME with Dr Fischer on February 20, report March 10 says says treatment is reasonable and ongoing. Alicia Romano is the worker\'s attorney. Hearing held February 20. Second hearing April 11.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 818, n.word_count = 138;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977160-082-C02'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977160-082', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 2, n.text = 'CURRENT MEDICAL: treating with Dr Haddad at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center. Pain was 0/10 at the last visit (April 3) and Chloe reports no complaints. Restrictions: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nWORK STATUS: Chloe is back to full duty.\nBENEFITS: no lost time, no wage benefits due at this point. Medical bills are being paid per the fee schedule.\nLEGAL: next hearing is on November 10, notice to employer and Alicia Romano.\nIME: Dr Fischer saw Chloe and the report says says treatment is reasonable and ongoing. We are reviewing whether to dispute any of the ongoing treatment.\nChloe is represented by Alicia Romano, who has asked for the claim file and our position on added treatment. We are responding by letter.\nCONTACTS: adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Frank Nakamura (City Operations Department), ER supervisor Ravi Brandt, treating Dr Haddad at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center.\nCOVERAGE: State Insurance Fund is on the risk. Claim is in Rockland county, injury location warehouse. No prior claims found on Chloe.\nOUTSTANDING: nothing.\nRESERVES: no change recommended right now, med reserve $12,000. We will revisit after the next medical report.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, speak with Chloe and employer again this month, and send the next update by May 8. Please let me know if you need anything else in the meantime.', n.char_start = 820, n.char_end = 2160, n.word_count = 221;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977160-082-C03'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977160-082', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 3, n.text = 'Thanks,\nDaniel Brooks', n.char_start = 2162, n.char_end = 2183, n.word_count = 3;
