MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-030-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-030', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'reserve review January 12: paid to date approx $15,000. we should revisit after the next medical. -CJ', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 101, n.word_count = 17;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-031-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-031', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = '1/13/26 outbound call to Camila. Said she slipped on a spill near the counter. Trouble sleeping because of the pain. Still hard to stand or walk for long. Cx says she is not sure she can do the light duty offered, I told her to talk to Dr Lindqvist. Wants to know if she has to go to the IME, told yes and the letter went out.\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho and Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 504, n.word_count = 100;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-032-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-032', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Spoke with Camila by phone. Cx confirmed DOI 12/15/25 at retail store.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 70, n.word_count = 12;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-033-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-033', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = '1/13/26 outbound call to Camila. Cx states knee swelling, feels unstable on stairs. Says she saw Dr Lindqvist on 1/6/26. Wants a copy of the C-3, will mail. Asked about the status of the claim, explained it is open. Taking tylenol as needed. Cx says she is not sure she can do the light duty offered, I told her to talk to Dr Lindqvist. Wants to know if she has to go to the IME, told yes and the letter went out. Next appt with Dr Lindqvist is 1/26. Will call back.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 466, n.word_count = 92;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-034-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-034', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Spoke with cx . Says she saw Dr Lindqvist on 1/6/26. Asked who pays for Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab visits, told Starbucks Corporation pays per fee schedule and to keep receipts. Wants a copy of the C-3, will mail. Asked about the status of the claim, explained it is open, no Board date yet. Worried about the employer cutting hours. Taking tylenol as needed. Back on light duty. Camila confirmed DOI 12/15/25 at retail store. Still hard to stand or walk for long. Cx says she is not sure she can do the light duty offered, I told her to talk to Dr Lindqvist. Wants to know if she has to go to the IME, told yes and the letter went out. Cx says Carla Brennan will call me. Next appt with Dr Lindqvist is 1/26. Will call back.\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 3 of 6 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered 1-6-2026, report still pending. Carla Brennan is the worker\'s attorney. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $620 paid to date. Contacts: Adjuster Olivia Grant, ER contact Dev Sato, ER supervisor Lena Haddad, treating Dr Lindqvist, PT Carla Castillo at Summit Rehab & Sports PT. Coverage: Starbucks Corporation on the risk, Nassau county, retail store. Still waiting on records from prior provider and MRI report.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 1455, n.word_count = 262;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-035-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-035', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Need to respond to this.\nFrom: Lena (front desk) <lena@hudsonvalleyorthorehab.example>\nSent: Mon, Jan 19, 2026 12:57\nTo: Olivia Grant\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977197 - Morris\n\nHi Olivia,\nCamila Morris is being seen for strain of the knee.\nWork status: working modified duty.\nAttached is the note from Camila Morris\'s visit on 1/6/26.\nNext visit is scheduled for 1/26.\n\nThanks,\nLena (front desk)', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 389, n.word_count = 62;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-036-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-036', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Rehab note January 21: Visit 4 of 6. Missed last appt, rescheduled. ROM: Knee/ankle ROM near full, some pain at end range.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 122, n.word_count = 22;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-037-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-037', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'STATUS: cx, left knee strain, DOI December 15. file is still open.\nMEDICAL: seeing Dr Lindqvist at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab; pain 7/10 per last note; pain at the front of the knee, catches.\nWORK: back on light duty; restr: no standing over 2 hrs, no ladders, no kneeling.\nPAY: no lost time, no wage payments, medical bills only.\nLEGAL: first hearing is on 2/24/26, notice went to all parties.\nPENDING: written light duty offer from the employer.\nPLAN: we get the written light duty offer from the employer, then close the diary 2/6/26.\nHISTORY: DOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started December 31, 4 of 6 authorized visits used so far.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 845, n.word_count = 152;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-038-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-038', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = '1/26/26 - auth note: MRI auth\'d Northeast Diagnostic Imaging to schedule. Waiting on the MRI report from Northeast Diagnostic Imaging.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 134, n.word_count = 20;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-039-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-039', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'From: Carol Jennings <carol@gbclaims.example>\nSent: Mon, Jan 26, 2026 17:17\nTo: Olivia Grant\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977197 - Morris\n\nHi Olivia,\nPlease confirm the reserve is still $4,500.\nPlease see the file for Camila Morris, claim 6977197.\nLet me know if you need authority for the PT visits.\nWe need the auth for more PT visits before the next review.\n\nRegards,\nCarol Jennings', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 376, n.word_count = 63;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-040-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-040', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'OFFICE NOTE (Dr Lindqvist): C-4.2 to follow.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 44, n.word_count = 7;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-041-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-041', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Rehab note visit 6 of 6. Pain 6/10 pre-tx, 6/10 after. Progressing w/ HEP. ROM: Knee/ankle ROM near full, some pain at end range. Goal: Stand a full shift without pain. Pt arrived early, no problems. Will reassess at visit 9.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 225, n.word_count = 41;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-042-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-042', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Need to respond to this.\nFrom: Beth (front desk) <beth@hudsonvalleyorthorehab.example>\nSent: Tue, Feb 3, 2026 12:28\nTo: Olivia Grant\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977197 - Morris\n\nHi Olivia,\nCamila Morris is being seen for strain of the knee.\nNext visit is scheduled for 2/11.\nWe are requesting 16 PT visits, please advise.\nPlease confirm authorization for the Rx.\n\nRegards,\nBeth (front desk)', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 382, n.word_count = 61;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-043-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-043', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'bill rvw (Olivia): Rx from Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab $211.00 reduced to fee schedule. still need', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 98, n.word_count = 17;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-044-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-044', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Carla Brennan called 2/10/26 re: Cx. Requesting copies of medical, wage statement and C-2F for claim 6977197. Asks status of the hearing before the judge. Wants to know if Starbucks Corporation will authorize more tx.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 217, n.word_count = 35;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-045-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-045', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Subject: Status Report - Claim 6977197 - Camila Morris\nHi Dana,\n\nPlease see the update below on Camila Morris\'s claim (MetroClean Services, DOI 12/15/25, retail store). I have kept the history short, call me if you want more.\n\nCLAIM HISTORY\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12-31-2025, 8 of 16 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered 1/6/26, result 1-18-2026: mild effusion, possible meniscus signal change. Carla Brennan is the worker\'s attorney. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $1,025 paid to date. Contacts: adjuster Olivia Grant, ER contact Dev Sato, ER supervisor Lena Haddad, treating Dr Lindqvist, PT Carla Castillo at Summit Rehab & Sports PT. Coverage: Starbucks Corporation on the risk, Nassau county, retail store.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 955, n.word_count = 157;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-045-C02'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-045', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 2, n.text = 'CURRENT MEDICAL: treating with Dr Lindqvist at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab. Pain was 6/10 at the last visit (1/26/26) and cx reports pain at the front of the knee, catches. Restrictions: no kneeling or squatting, limited stairs.\nWORK STATUS: cx is working w/ restrictions.\nBENEFITS: no lost time, no wage benefits due at this point. Medical bills are being paid per the fee schedule.\nLEGAL: first hearing is on February 24, notice went to all parties.\ncx is represented by Carla Brennan, who has asked for the claim file and our position on added treatment. We are responding by letter.\nCONTACTS: adjuster Olivia Grant, ER contact Dev Sato (MetroClean Services), ER supervisor Lena Haddad, treating Dr Lindqvist at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab. PT is Carla Castillo at Summit Rehab & Sports PT.\nCOVERAGE: Starbucks Corporation is on the risk. Claim is in Nassau county, injury location retail store. No prior claims found on cx.\nOUTSTANDING: nothing.\nRESERVES: no change recommended right now, med reserve $12,000. We will revisit after the next medical report.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, speak with cx and the employer again this month, and send the next update by 2/24/26. Please let me know if you need anything else in the meantime.\n\nThanks,\nOlivia Grant', n.char_start = 957, n.char_end = 2214, n.word_count = 210;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-046-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-046', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'February 11 checked eCase, nothing new. Cx working modified duty.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 65, n.word_count = 10;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-047-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-047', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Rehab note February 13: Visit 9 of 16. Tolerated tx well. Did quad sets, straight leg raises, step-ups, stationary bike + ice. ROM: Knee/ankle ROM near full, some pain at end range. Pt arrived late, shortened session. Reviewed HEP, pt demonstrates correctly.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 258, n.word_count = 42;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-048-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-048', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Dr note rec\'d 02/13/2026 from Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab: Meds: Tylenol prn. Pt asks about stand or walk for long advised to modify.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 133, n.word_count = 24;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-049-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-049', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Legal note 2/13/26: First hearing is on 2/24/26, notice went to all parties. Cx asked if she has to attend - told to check the notice. Olivia aware. Nothing else scheduled that I can see. The IME report needs to be in by then.\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 9 of 16 authorized visits used so far.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 522, n.word_count = 99;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-050-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-050', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'February 17 therapy session #10 - Carla Castillo, PT. Pain 6/10 pre-tx, 5/10 after. Strength 4-/5. Pt asked if more visits will be approved.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 140, n.word_count = 24;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-051-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-051', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'STATUS: cx, left knee strain, DOI 12/15/25. file is still open.\nMEDICAL: seeing Dr Lindqvist at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab; pain 6/10 per last note; knee sore, swelling after standing.\nWORK: back on light duty; restr: no kneeling or squatting, limited stairs.\nPAY: no lost time, no wage payments, medical bills only.\nLEGAL: first hearing is on 2/24/26, notice went to all parties.\nPENDING: nothing.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, next review 3/6/26.\nHISTORY: DOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 10 of 16 authorized visits used so far.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 752, n.word_count = 129;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-052-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-052', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = '2/20/26 - RTW: Cx is back on light duty. Restr per Dr Lindqvist: No kneeling or squatting, limited stairs. Cx did 3 days of modified duty then called out. Dev Sato says light duty available, hours reduced. Full duty release expected 3/11. Asked Dr Lindqvist for updated work status. The employer should have the new restrictions in writing.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 340, n.word_count = 58;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-053-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-053', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Spoke with cx 20FEB26. Wants a copy of the C-3, will mail. Asked if Olivia is still the adjuster, confirmed. Wants too know if she has to go to the IME, told yes and the letter went out.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 186, n.word_count = 38;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-054-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-054', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = '2/24/26: ECase check - hearing held 2/24/26, adjourned for the attorney to submit position. Claim 6977197, hearing before the judge. Copy to Starbucks Corporation and the employer. Nothing else scheduled that I can see. The IME report needs to be in by then.\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 11 of 16 authorized visits used so far.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 555, n.word_count = 98;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-055-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-055', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'February 25 therapy session #12 - Carla Castillo, PT. Tolerated tx well. Pt reports pain at the front of the knee, catches. Pain 6/10 pre-tx, 5/10 after. Did quad sets, straight leg raises, step-ups, stationary bike + ice. Progressing w/ HEP. ROM: Knee/ankle ROM near full, some pain at end range. Strength 4/5. Goal: Stand a full shift without pain. Pt asked if more visits will be approved. Reviewed HEP, pt demonstrates correctly. Pt arrived early, no problems.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 464, n.word_count = 78;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-056-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-056', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'February 25: ECase check - hearing held 2/24/26, adjourned for IME report. Claim 6977197, hearing before the judge. Copy to Starbucks Corporation and the employer. Cx asked if she has to attend - told to check the notice. Olivia aware. Nothing else scheduled that I can see. Cx notified by letter. The IME report needs to be in by then.\nDOI 12/15/25, cx slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 12 of 16 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered 1/6/26, result January 18: Mild effusion, possible meniscus signal change. Carla Brennan is the worker\'s attorney. Hearing held 2/24/26. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $1,360 paid to date. Contacts: Adjuster Olivia Grant, ER contact Dev Sato, ER supervisor Lena Haddad, treating Dr Lindqvist, PT Carla Castillo at Summit Rehab & Sports PT. Coverage: Starbucks Corporation on the risk, Nassau county, retail store.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 1073, n.word_count = 181;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-057-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-057', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Peer review rec\'d 2/25/26 (Dr Doyle). Purpose: Causation + need for further tx for knee. Cx not happy with the exam, says it lasted 10 min. Dr Lindqvist may disagree. Report due approx 2 wks after the exam. Camila told to bring imaging and ID.\nDOI 12/15/25, Camila slipped on a spill near the counter at retail store. First seen at Hudson Valley Ortho & Rehab on 12/18/25, dx strain of the left knee, xray neg for fracture. On modified duty from 12/17/25. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 12/31/25, 12 of 16 authorized visits used so far.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 544, n.word_count = 100;
MERGE (n:Chunk {chunk_id: 'SYN-6977197-058-C01'}) SET n.parent_id = 'SYN-6977197-058', n.parent_kind = 'Note', n.position = 1, n.text = 'Therapy session #13 - Carla Castillo, PT. Tolerated tx well. Pt reports pain at the front of the knee, catches. Pain 6/10 pre-tx, 5/10 after. Did quad sets, straight leg raises, step-ups, stationary bike + ice. Progressing w/ HEP. Missed last appt, rescheduled. ROM: Knee/ankle ROM near full, some pain at end range. Strength 4+/5. Goal: Stand a full shift without pain. Pt asked if more visits will be approved. Cont plan of care.', n.char_start = 0, n.char_end = 431, n.word_count = 74;
