MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977121-071'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977121', n.note_date = '2026-04-23', n.note_type = 'Status Report', n.author_name = 'Daniel Brooks', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'Subject: Status Report - Claim 6977121 - Leo Morgan\nHi Tom,\n\nPlease see the update below on Leo Morgan\'s claim (Lakeside Coffee Retail, DOI 19DEC25, warehouse). I have kept the history short, call me if you want more.\n\nCLAIM HISTORY\nDOI December 19, Leo Morgan was repositioning stock and felt a pull at warehouse. First seen at Capital Region Occupational Health on December 24, dx strain of the neck, upper back and shoulder, xray neg. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $630 paid to date. Contacts: adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Victor Alvarez, ER supervisor Alicia Whitaker, treating Dr Lindqvist. Coverage: HARTFORD CASUALTY INSURANCE CO on the risk, Queens county, warehouse.\n\nCURRENT MEDICAL: treating with Dr Lindqvist at Capital Region Occupational Health. Pain was 0/10 at the last visit (3-26-2026) and Leo reports mild stiffness only. Restrictions: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nWORK STATUS: Leo is back to full duty.\nBENEFITS: no lost time, no wage benefits due at this point. Medical bills are being paid per the fee schedule.\nLEGAL: no hearings or conciliation set, nothing from the Board that needs a response.\nCONTACTS: adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Victor Alvarez (Lakeside Coffee Retail), ER supervisor Alicia Whitaker, treating Dr Lindqvist at Capital Region Occupational Health.\nCOVERAGE: HARTFORD CASUALTY INSURANCE CO is on the risk. Claim is in Queens county, injury location warehouse. No prior claims found on Leo.\nOUTSTANDING: nothing.\nRESERVES: no change recommended right now, med reserve $15,000. We will revisit after the next medical report.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, speak with Leo and employer again this month, and send the next update by May 14. Please let me know if you need anything else in the meantime.\n\nThanks,\nDaniel Brooks', n.word_count = 286, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977121-072'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977121', n.note_date = '2026-04-27', n.note_type = 'Reserve Review', n.author_name = 'Carol Jennings', n.author_role = 'supervisor', n.text = 'April 27 reserves - Daniel\'s file: increased med reserve bc MRI ordered ok to send the status report we should revisit after next medical -CJ', n.word_count = 25, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
