MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-103'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-06-25', n.note_type = 'File Review', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'STATUS: Emma, low back, hip and both knees strain, DOI 12/21/2025. file is still open.\nMEDICAL: seeing DR Haddad at North Shore Occupational Health; pain 2/10 per last note; sore all over, stiff in the mornings.\nWORK: back to full duty; restr: lifting up to 30 lbs ok, no prolonged bending.\nPAY: no lost time, no wage payments, medical bills only.\nLEGAL: judge\'s decision rec\'d after the 04/14/2026 hearing, nothing more needed from us.\nPENDING: nothing.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, next review 07/16/2026.\nHISTORY: DOI 12/21/25, IW missed the last few steps and fell at operations facility. First seen at North Shore Occupational Health on 12/25/2025, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. Off work from 12/22/2025. On modified duty from 01/15/2026. Back to full duty from 05/30/2026. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 01/06/2026, 16 of 16 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered 1/12/26, result 01/24/2026: mild disc bulge L4-5, no stenosis. IME with Dr Iyer on 03/05/2026, report 03/20/2026 says supports a work-related injury, no ongoing disability. Lena Alvarez is the worker\'s attorney. Hearing held 03/03/2026. Second hearing 04/14/2026. Weekly payments of $710 started 12/31/2025, approx $17,750 paid to date. Contacts: adjuster Marcus Hill, ER contact Tasha Kowalski, ER supervisor Greg Romano, treating DR Haddad, PT Lena Mehta at Summit Rehab & Sports PT. Coverage: State Ins Fund on the risk, Queens county, operations facility.', n.word_count = 238, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-104'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-06-30', n.note_type = 'Attorney Correspondence', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'need to respond to this -MH\nFrom: Lena Alvarez <lena@alvarezlaw.example>\nSent: Tue, Jun 30, 2026 17:16\nTo: Marcus Hill\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977156 - Rivera\n\nHi Marcus,\nPlease provide a copy of the IME report.\nMy client is available for a call, my office number is on file.\n\nRegards,\nLena Alvarez', n.word_count = 51, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = true, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-105'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-09', n.note_type = 'Reserve Review', n.author_name = 'Carol Jennings', n.author_role = 'supervisor', n.text = 'July 9 reserves - Marcus\'s file: paid to date approx $4,500.', n.word_count = 11, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-106'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-10', n.note_type = 'Bill Question', n.author_name = 'Tina Morales', n.author_role = 'assistant', n.text = 'bill review office visit from North Shore Occ Health $135.50 pnded for records. -Tina', n.word_count = 14, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-107'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-13', n.note_type = 'Status Report', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'Subject: Status Report - Claim 6977156 - Emma Rivera\nHi Tom,\n\nPlease see the update below on Emma Rivera\'s claim (Harborview Community Health, DOI 12/21/2025, operations facility). I have kept the history short, call me if you want more.\n\nCLAIM HISTORY\nDOI 12/21/2025, IW missed the last few steps and fell at operations facility. First seen at North Shore Occupational Health on 12/25/2025, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. Off work from 12/22/2025. On modified duty from 01/15/2026. Back to full duty from 05/30/2026. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started 01/06/2026, 16 of 16 authorized visits used so far. MRI ordered 01/12/2026, result 01/24/2026: mild disc bulge L4-5, no stenosis. IME with Dr Iyer on 03/05/2026, report 03/20/2026 says supports a work-related injury, no ongoing disability. Lena Alvarez is the worker\'s attorney.\n\nCURRENT MEDICAL: treating with DR Haddad at North Shore Occupational Health. Pain was 0/10 at the last visit (06/08/2026) and IW reports mild stiffness only. Restrictions: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nWORK STATUS: IW is back to full duty.\nBENEFITS: no lost time, no wage benefits due at this point. Medical bills are being paid per the fee schedule.\nLEGAL: second hearing 04/14/2026 held, judge reserved decision.\nIME: Dr Iyer saw IW and the report says supports a work-related injury, no ongoing disability. We are reviewing whether to dispute any of the ongoing treatment.\nEmma is represented by Lena Alvarez, who has asked for the claim file and our position on added treatment. We are responding by letter.\nCONTACTS: adjuster Marcus Hill, ER contact Tasha Kowalski (Harborview Community Health), ER supervisor Greg Romano, treating DR Haddad at North Shore Occupational Health. PT is Lena Mehta at Summit Rehab & Sports PT.\nCOVERAGE: SIF is on the risk. Claim is in Queens county, injury location operations facility. No prior claims found on IW.\nOUTSTANDING: nothing.\nRESERVES: no change recommended right now, med reserve $12,000. We will revisit after the next medical report.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, speak with IW and employer again this month, and send the next update by 08/12/2026. Please let me know if you need anything else in the meantime.\n\nThanks,\nMarcus Hill', n.word_count = 369, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-108'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-21', n.note_type = 'Authorization', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'FORWARDING TO FILE. -MH\nFrom: Lena (front desk) <lena@northshoreoccupationalhealth.example>\nSent: Tue, Jul 21, 2026 12:46\nTo: Marcus Hill\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977156 - Rivera\n\nHi Marcus,\nRestrictions remain: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nWe are requesting 16 PT visits, please advise.\nEmma Rivera is being seen for strain of the low back, hip and both knees.\n\nThank you,\nLena (front desk)', n.word_count = 62, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = true, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-109'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-24', n.note_type = 'Attorney Correspondence', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'see below -MH\nFrom: Lena Alvarez <lena@alvarezlaw.example>\nSent: Fri, Jul 24, 2026 15:12\nTo: Marcus Hill\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977156 - Rivera\n\nHi Marcus,\nKindly confirm SIF\'s position on the low back, hip and both knees treatment.\nThe nothing is still outstanding on our end.\n\nThank you,\nLena Alvarez', n.word_count = 49, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = true, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-110'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-07-27', n.note_type = 'File Review', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'STATUS: IW, low back, hip and both knnees strain, DOI 12/21/2025. file is still open.\nMEDICAL: seeing DR Haddad at North Shore Occupational Health; pain 0/10 per last note; mild stiffness only.\nWORK: back to full duty; restr: released to full duty, no restrictons.\nPAY: no lost time, no wage payments, medical bills only.\nLEGAL: judge\'s decision rec\'d after the 04/14/2026 hearing, nothing more needed from us.\nPENDING: nothing.\nPLAN: we get the nothing, then close the diary 08/26/2026.', n.word_count = 79, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-111'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-08-17', n.note_type = 'Attorney Correspondence', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'forwarding to file.\nFrom: Lena Alvarez <lena@alvarezlaw.example>\nSent: Mon, Aug 17, 2026 14:24\nTo: Marcus Hill\nSubject: RE: Claim 6977156 - Rivera\n\nHi Marcus,\nPlease provide a copy of the IME report.\nWe request authorization for the treatment recommended by DR Haddad.\nMy client has not been paid for Rx, please advise.\n\nThanks,\nLena Alvarez', n.word_count = 55, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = true, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-112'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-08-31', n.note_type = 'File Review', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'STATUS: IW, low back, hip and both knees strain, DOI 12/21/2025. file is open.\nMEDICAL: seeing DR Haddad at North Shore Occupational Health; pain 0/10 per last note; feeling much better, occasional soreness.\nWORK: working regular duty, no issues; restr: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nPAY: no lost time, no wage payments, medical bills only.\nLEGAL: second hearing 4-14-2026 held, judge reserved decision.\nPENDING: nothing.\nPLAN: call IW, follow up with DR Haddad, review again 09/21/2026.\nHISTORY: DOI 12/21/2025, IW missed the last few steps and fell at operations facility. First seen at North Shore Occupational Health on 12/25/2025, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. Off work from 12/22/2025. On modified duty from 01/15/2026.', n.word_count = 124, n.has_copied_history = false, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-113'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-09-15', n.note_type = 'Closure / Reopen', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'closing note 09/15/2026: IW back to full duty since 06/08/2026, no f/u needed. treated at North Shore Occupational Health, released, no restrictions. if IW calls w/ a flare up, reopen and send back to DR Haddad. all bills paid, nothing pending. final med report rec\'d, strain resolved. total paid on file approx $4,500.\nDOI 12/21/2025, IW missed the last few steps and fell at operations facility. first seen at North Shore Occupational Health on 12/25/2025, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. -MH', n.word_count = 91, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977156-114'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977156', n.note_date = '2026-09-21', n.note_type = 'Closure / Reopen', n.author_name = 'Marcus Hill', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'closing review: IW back to full duty since 06/08/2026, no f/u needed. Board closed the case, nothing open. no activity in 60 days, closing diary. treated at North Shore Occupational Health, released, no restrictions. if Emma calls w/ flare up, reopen and send back to DR Haddad. all bills paid, nothing pending. final med report rec\'d, strain resolved. total paid on the file approx $12,000.\nDOI 12/21/2025, IW missed last few steps and fell at operations facility. first seen at North Shore Occupational Health on 12/25/2025, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings -MH', n.word_count = 102, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
