MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977160-061'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977160', n.note_date = '2026-03-10', n.note_type = 'IME Note', n.author_name = 'Daniel Brooks', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'Peer review rec\'d 10MAR26 (Dr Fischer). Purpose: Causation + need for further tx for low back, hip and both knees. IME report in: Says tx is reasonable and ongoing. Chloe not happy with the exam, says it lasted 10 min. Dr Haddad may disagree. Need to decide if we dispute. Chloe told to bring imaging and ID. IME fee $22,000.\nDOI December 9, Chloe was hit at an intersection driving the company vehicle at warehouse. First seen at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center on December 12, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. On modified duty from December 10. Back to full duty from February 18. MRI ordered January 7, result January 18: Mild disc bulge L4-5, no stenosis. IME with Dr Fischer on February 20, report March 10 says says tx is reasonable and ongoing. Alicia Romano is the worker\'s attorney. Hearing held 20FEB26. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $575 paid to date. Contacts: Adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Frank Nakamura, ER supervisor Ravi Brandt, treating Dr Haddad. Coverage: State Insurance Fund on the risk, Rockland county, warehouse.', n.word_count = 189, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977160-062'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977160', n.note_date = '2026-03-11', n.note_type = 'File Review', n.author_name = 'Daniel Brooks', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'File review March 11. Chloe has a strain of the low back, hip and both knees from 12-9-2025, claim is scheduled for a hearing. Chloe is seeing Dr Haddad at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center and last reported pain at 3/10, pain in the low back, worse by end of shift. Restr are: Lifting up to 30 lbs ok, no prolonged bending. Chloe is working regular duty, no issues. No lost time and no wage payments due. Pending: Nothing. Plan: Call Chloe, follow up with Dr Haddad, review again 04/01/2026.\nDOI December 9, Chloe was hit at an intersection driving the company vehicle at warehouse. First seen at Upstate Hearing & Balance Center on December 12, dx strain of the low back, hip and both knees, lumbar xray no acute findings. On modified duty from December 10. Back to full duty from February 18.', n.word_count = 144, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
