MERGE (n:Note {note_id: 'SYN-6977194-076'}) SET n.claim_id = '6977194', n.note_date = '2026-04-06', n.note_type = 'Status Report', n.author_name = 'Daniel Brooks', n.author_role = 'adjuster', n.text = 'Subject: Status Report - Claim 6977194 - Naomi Bailey\nHi Ravi,\n\nPlease see the update below on Naomi Bailey\'s claim (Albany Public Works, DOI June 29, warehouse). I have kept the history short, call me if you want more.\n\nCLAIM HISTORY\nDOI June 29, Naomi Bailey got grabbed by another person during a transfer at warehouse. First seen at Capital Region Occupational Health on November 24, dx strain of the right knee, xray neg for fracture. PT at Summit Rehab & Sports PT started December 3, 12 of 12 authorized visits used so far. No wage payments, medical bills only, approx $1,415 paid to date. Contacts: adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Frank Kowalski, ER supervisor Dev Alvarez, treating Dr Fischer, PT Joan Haddad at Summit Rehab & Sports PT. Coverage: SIF on the risk, Warren county, warehouse.\n\nCURRENT MEDICAL: treating with Dr Fischer at Capital Region Occupational Health. Pain was 0/10 at the last visit (February 16) and Naomi reports feeling much better, occasional soreness. Restrictions: released to full duty, no restrictions.\nWORK STATUS: Naomi is back to full duty.\nBENEFITS: no lost time, no wage benefits due at this point. Medical bills are being paid per the fee schedule.\nLEGAL: no hearings or conciliation set, nothing from the Board that needs a response.\nCONTACTS: adjuster Daniel Brooks, ER contact Frank Kowalski (Albany Public Works), ER supervisor Dev Alvarez, treating Dr Fischer at Capital Region Occupational Health. PT is Joan Haddad at Summit Rehab & Sports PT.\nCOVERAGE: SIF is on the risk. Claim is in Warren county, injury location warehouse. No prior claims found on Naomi.\nOUTSTANDING: nothing.\nRESERVES: no change recommended right now, med reserve $12,000. We will revisit after the next medical report.\nPLAN: continue to monitor, speak with Naomi and employer again this month, and send the next update by 4/27/26. Please let me know if you need anything else in the meantime.\n\nThanks,\nDaniel Brooks', n.word_count = 320, n.has_copied_history = true, n.has_pasted_email = false, n.looks_truncated = false;
